# Move the end effector by a Cartesian offset (dx, dy, dz) from its CURRENT
# pose, holding orientation fixed. A general single-move primitive — used by
# TaskOrchestrator's inspect_object to pull a held object horizontally away
# from a nearby obstacle before rotating it, WITHOUT driving the robot base
# (dz=0 for that use). Collision-aware OFF, same reasoning as the existing
# post-grasp retreat: moving away from a neighbour cannot collide with it.
float64 dx
float64 dy
float64 dz
float64 move_time   # seconds; <= 0 uses a sensible default
---
bool success
string message
geometry_msgs/Point ee_position   # where the EE ended up, for the caller's own bookkeeping
